   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "propagation over 4 years formed the variety \u2018Autumn\nBlue\u2019",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
  {
   "bbox": [
    300.48,
    77.76,
    537.6,
    234.24
   ],
   "id": "e14",
   "lines": [
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      77.76,
      456.96,
      86.4
     ],
     "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables."
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      87.84,
      519.36,
      96.48
     ],
     "text": "\u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 is a compact, upright, herbaceous plant"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      97.92,
      507.84,
      106.56
     ],
     "text": "which flowers during autumn, winter and spring. In"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      108.0,
      516.96,
      116.64
     ],
     "text": "comparison, the blue form of Lechenaultia biloba, and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      118.08,
      531.84,
      126.72
     ],
     "text": "\"White Flash\u2019, flower only in spring. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 leaves"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      127.68,
      527.04,
      136.32
     ],
     "text": "are the same width as the comparative varieties, but are"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      137.76,
      533.28,
      144.96
     ],
     "text": "shorter than those of \u2018White Flash\u2019. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 has an"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      147.84,
      530.4,
      156.48
     ],
     "text": "upright growth habit in contrast to the semi-erect growth"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      157.44,
      530.4,
      166.08
     ],
     "text": "habit of the comparative varieties. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 flowers"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      167.04,
      535.2,
      175.68
     ],
     "text": "are narrower in diameter and shorter in height and corolla"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      177.12,
      528.96,
      185.76
     ],
     "text": "length than the comparative varieties. The newly opened"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      187.2,
      521.28,
      195.36
     ],
     "text": "flowers of \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 are slightly darker violet-blue"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.96,
      196.8,
      519.36,
      205.44
     ],
     "text": "than the comparative varieties, and when fully opened"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      206.88,
      514.08,
      215.52
     ],
     "text": "they are blue. The aged flowers of \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 are"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      300.48,
      216.96,
      537.6,
      224.64
     ],
     "text": "violet-blue, whereas those of the blue form of L. biloba and"
    },
    {
     "bbox": [
      301.44,
      227.52,
      390.24,
      234.24
     ],
     "text": "\u2018White Flash\u2019 are blue."
    }
   ],
   "page": 1,
   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Morphology \u2014 see comparison tables.\n\u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 is a compact, upright, herbaceous plant\nwhich flowers during autumn, winter and spring. In\ncomparison, the blue form of Lechenaultia biloba, and\n\"White Flash\u2019, flower only in spring. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 leaves\nare the same width as the comparative varieties, but are\nshorter than those of \u2018White Flash\u2019. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 has an\nupright growth habit in contrast to the semi-erect growth\nhabit of the comparative varieties. \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 flowers\nare narrower in diameter and shorter in height and corolla\nlength than the comparative varieties. The newly opened\nflowers of \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 are slightly darker violet-blue\nthan the comparative varieties, and when fully opened\nthey are blue. The aged flowers of \u2018Autumn Blue\u2019 are\nviolet-blue, whereas those of the blue form of L. biloba and\n\u2018White Flash\u2019 are blue.",
   "text_format": "plain",
   "type": "text"
  },
